# 🌳 Binary Trees (Part 1) - Introduction & Tree Traversals

## 📌 Introduction

A **Tree** is a non-linear data structure that represents data in a hierarchical form.

Unlike arrays and linked lists, trees do not store elements sequentially.

A **Binary Tree** is a tree in which each node can have at most **two children**:

- Left Child
- Right Child

Binary Trees are one of the most important topics in DSA and form the foundation for BSTs, Heaps, and many advanced tree problems.

